# Tables

`[name] := table` followed by a Markdown table gives typed columns.

[groceries] := table
| item  | quantity | price |
| ----- | -------- | ----- |
| apple | 2        | $3.30 |
| pear  | 4        | $4.30 |

[total] := sum(groceries, quantity * price)
[units] := sum(groceries, quantity)
[average] := total / units

Groceries cost [total] for [units] items, [average] each.

<!-- Columns keep one type; a bad cell is reported at the cell. Hover a column
for a sparkline, the sum for row contributions. Rename a column to update
formulas. Try: Format Document to align the table. -->
